### F6 — Sparse `_get_finite_row_indices` misclassifies rows containing non-finite non-stored patterns
severity: low
evidence: sklearn/cluster/_hdbscan/hdbscan.py:401-404 uses `matrix.tolil().data` which only exposes explicit non-zero entries. A row whose only non-finite value is an explicitly-stored zero-eliminated position (or whose finiteness is encoded through structural zeros meaning "no distance") will not be considered non-finite.
scenario: "user builds a CSR distance matrix, marks a missing distance as `np.inf` but does not store the inf explicitly (or `eliminate_zeros()` was applied and a nan appears as an eliminated slot) → the row is treated as fully finite and the point is not tagged as an outlier"
contract: detect non-finite entries via `np.isfinite(matrix.data)` grouped by row (using indptr), so any explicitly stored non-finite value in a CSR row marks the row.
